 {"name": "IsLocalization.AwayCover.picClass_map_refine", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem picClass_map_refine [Module.FaithfullyFlat A (\u2200 i, S i)] [Module.FaithfullyFlat A (\u2200 i', S' i')] {\u03b3 : \u2200 i j, (T i j)\u02e3} {\u03b3' : \u2200 i' j', (T' i' j')\u02e3} (h\u03b3 : IsCoverCocycle (f := f) (S := S) (W := W) \u03b3) (h\u03b3' : IsCoverCocycle (f := f') (S := S') (W := W') \u03b3') (hrel : \u2200 i' j', \u03b3' i' j' = Units.map (refineOverlapAlgHom f T T' \u03c4 h\u03c4T i' j').toRingHom.toMonoidHom (\u03b3 (\u03c4 i') (\u03c4 j'))) : (isDescentCocycle_cocycleUnit f' S' T' W' h\u03b3').picClass = (isDescentCocycle_cocycleUnit f S T W h\u03b3).picClass", "doc": "**Refinement invariance of the Picard class**: restricting a cover cocycle along a refinement of finite localization covers does not change the Picard class of the descended module.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Algebra/LocalizationCocycleRefine.lean", "line": 210}
