+{"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.quotEquivMapPow", "kind": "def", "signature": "noncomputable def quotEquivMapPow {I : Ideal B} (h : I.IsPrincipal) (h' : I \u2260 \u22a5) (n : \u2115) : (B \u29f8 I) \u2243\u2097[k] (Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ (n + 1))) (I ^ n))", "doc": "The `k`-linear iso `B \u29f8 I \u2243\u2097[k] I ^ n \u29f8 I ^ (n+1)`, realised as the image ideal `(I ^ n).map (mk (I ^ (n+1)))` inside `B \u29f8 I ^ (n+1)`.     * Provenance: CUSTOM.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Algebra/DedekindColength.lean", "line": 148}
+{"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.finrank_quotient_pow_succ", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem finrank_quotient_pow_succ {I : Ideal B} (h : I.IsPrincipal) (h' : I \u2260 \u22a5) (n : \u2115) [Module.Finite k (B \u29f8 I ^ (n + 1))] [Module.Finite k (B \u29f8 I ^ n)] : finrank k (B \u29f8 I ^ (n + 1)) = finrank k (B \u29f8 I) + finrank k (B \u29f8 I ^ n)", "doc": "**Inductive step of the colength formula.**  For a nonzero principal ideal `I`, `finrank k (B \u29f8 I ^ (n+1)) = finrank k (B \u29f8 I) + finrank k (B \u29f8 I ^ n)`.     * Provenance: CUSTOM.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Algebra/DedekindColength.lean", "line": 161}
+{"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.finrank_quotient_span_pow_aux", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "private theorem finrank_quotient_span_pow_aux {I : Ideal B} (h : I.IsPrincipal) (h' : I \u2260 \u22a5) : \u2200 e : \u2115, Module.Finite k (B \u29f8 I ^ e) \u2192 finrank k (B \u29f8 I ^ e) = e \u2022 finrank k (B \u29f8 I)", "doc": "Auxiliary induction for `finrank_quotient_span_pow`, threading finiteness explicitly.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Algebra/DedekindColength.lean", "line": 186}
+{"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.finrank_quotient_span_pow", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem finrank_quotient_span_pow {I : Ideal B} (h : I.IsPrincipal) (h' : I \u2260 \u22a5) (e : \u2115) [Module.Finite k (B \u29f8 I ^ e)] : finrank k (B \u29f8 I ^ e) = e \u2022 finrank k (B \u29f8 I)", "doc": "**Prime-power / DVR colength formula.**  For a nonzero principal ideal `I = (\u03c0)` in `B` whose quotient `B \u29f8 I ^ e` is finite over the base field `k`, the `k`-dimension of `B \u29f8 I ^ e` is `e` copies of the residue dimension: `finrank k (B \u29f8 I ^ e) = e \u2022 finrank k (B \u29f8 I)`.     * Provenance: CUSTOM.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Algebra/DedekindColength.lean", "line": 215}
+{"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.quotAlgEquivPiFactors", "kind": "def", "signature": "noncomputable def quotAlgEquivPiFactors {I : Ideal B} (hI : I \u2260 \u22a5) : (B \u29f8 I) \u2243\u2090[k] (\u2200 P : (factors I).toFinset, B \u29f8 (P : Ideal B) ^ Multiset.count (P : Ideal B) (factors I))", "doc": "The Chinese remainder theorem for a Dedekind domain, upgraded to a `k`-algebra equivalence: `B \u29f8 I \u2243\u2090[k] \u220f_P B \u29f8 P ^ (mult of P in I)`.     * Provenance: CUSTOM.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Algebra/DedekindColength.lean", "line": 238}
+{"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.finrank_quotient_eq_sum_factors_pow", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem finrank_quotient_eq_sum_factors_pow {I : Ideal B} (hI : I \u2260 \u22a5) [\u2200 P : (factors I).toFinset, Module.Finite k (B \u29f8 (P : Ideal B) ^ Multiset.count (P : Ideal B) (factors I))] : finrank k (B \u29f8 I) = \u2211 P : (factors I).toFinset, finrank k (B \u29f8 (P : Ideal B) ^ Multiset.count (P : Ideal B) (factors I))", "doc": "**Multi-prime colength via the Chinese remainder theorem.**  For a nonzero ideal `I` of a Dedekind domain `B`, finite over the base field `k`, the `k`-dimension of `B \u29f8 I` is the sum, over the prime factors `P` of `I`, of the `k`-dimensions of the prime-power quotients `B \u29f8 P ^ (mult of P in I)`.     * Provenance: CUSTOM.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Algebra/DedekindColength.lean", "line": 261}
+{"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.finrank_quotient_span_eq_sum_ord", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem finrank_quotient_span_eq_sum_ord {f : B} (hf : f \u2260 0) (hprin : \u2200 P : (factors (Ideal.span {f})).toFinset, (P : Ideal B).IsPrincipal) [\u2200 P : (factors (Ideal.span {f})).toFinset, Module.Finite k (B \u29f8 (P : Ideal B) ^ Multiset.count (P : Ideal B) (factors (Ideal.span {f})))] : finrank k (B \u29f8 Ideal.span {f}) = \u2211 P : (factors (Ideal.span {f})).toFinset, Multiset.count (P : Ideal B) (factors (Ideal.span {f})) \u2022 finrank k (B \u29f8 (P : Ideal B))", "doc": "**Dedekind colength formula (ord-weighted form).**  For `f \u2260 0` in a Dedekind domain `B` whose height-one-prime factors are principal (e.g. `B` a PID) and whose prime-power residues are finite over the base field `k`, the `k`-dimension of `B \u29f8 (f)` is `\u2211_P (ord_P f) \u2022 finrank k (B \u29f8 P)`, the sum ranging over the prime factors of `(f)` with `ord_P f` the multiplicity of `P` in the factorization.     * Provenance: CUSTOM.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Algebra/DedekindColength.lean", "line": 280}
