 {"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.isUnit_one_add_C_mul_of_sqZero", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem isUnit_one_add_C_mul_of_sqZero {e : A} (he : e * e = 0) (p : Polynomial A) : IsUnit (1 + Polynomial.C e * p)", "doc": "**A square-zero deformation of `1` is a unit of the chart ring** `A[X]`, over an arbitrary commutative ring: `(1 + C e * p)(1 - C e * p) = 1` because the cross term carries `e\u00b2`.  This is the supply of chart units that `Polynomial.isUnit_iff` cannot see, and the reason that lemma needs a domain: at `e \u2260 0` this unit is not a constant.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Algebra/LaurentNilpotentCoboundary.lean", "line": 109}
